# Copy this to .env beside it and fill in what applies. The .env is
# git-ignored; this example is not, so never put a real licence in here.
#
# Nothing below is required. With no .env the backend uses HiGHS, which needs
# no licence and solves the campus in about 2.5 seconds a day.

# Which solver the optimizer asks Pyomo for.
#   appsi_highs   the default, bundled, no licence
#   gurobi        needs a licence below, or one already installed on this machine
ECOM_SOLVER=appsi_highs

# --- Gurobi, if you have a licence ----------------------------------------
#
# Either point at a licence file you already have:
#
# GRB_LICENSE_FILE=C:\Users\you\gurobi.lic
#
# or paste a Web License Service licence from the Gurobi portal, and the
# backend writes the file for you (into cache/gurobi/, also git-ignored):
#
# WLSACCESSID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# WLSSECRET=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# LICENSEID=0000000

# --- live battery readings, AWL -------------------------------------------
#
# The EHUB gateway on the Chalmers network, which publishes what the real
# battery is doing. Read-only here; commands are sent by hand from the
# notebook, not by the dashboard. Leave these out and the dashboard simply
# shows no live panel.
#
# The gateway's address is on the Chalmers network and is deliberately not
# written here - this file is public. Ask the EHUB owners for it.
# EHUB_URL=http://<gateway-host>:8090/api/v1
# EHUB_USER=
# EHUB_PASSWORD=
